ings from observed coding identity. If observations are\nabsent, say \"current OpenCode coding model\". Never claim the specialist ran from\nconfiguration alone. The coding manager keeps implementation; no global coding\nmodel changes.\n\nCall `flow_plan_approve` with a fresh operation id/current revision only after\nexplicit approval or prior autonomous implementation authority. Approval locks\nthe plan. Existing autonomous authority needs no additional approval. Ask\nconversational `/flow-auto` approval without requiring a second command; a reply\nmay resume its same process-local interaction only after approval advances the\nsame Flow session.\n\n`Plan only`/`do not implement yet` controls timing, not scope, and is never a\nplan requirement, decision, or non-goal. Do not implement or create a plan\ndocument unless requested.\n","sessionIndex":0,"status":"completed","tool":"flow_guidance"},{"agent":"build","input":{"request":{"expectedRevision":0,"goal":"Make parse(input) safely handle null and preserve trimmed strings, changing only src/parser.mjs and keeping node scripts/verify.mjs and its script unchanged.","operationId":"plan-null-parser","plan":{"decisions":["README.md declares node scripts/verify.mjs as the repository gate; it directly checks null and trimmed string behavior.","Use a strict null guard to preserve existing behavior for all other input types.","Existing untracked opencode.json is outside the implementation scope and will be preserved."],"evidence":[{"assertions":[],"command":"node scripts/verify.mjs","environment":"Current Linux workspace with Node.js","platform":"linux","requirement":"Null handling and string trimming pass the unchanged repository gate.","scope":"gate"}],"features":[{"dependsOn":[],"id":"null-safe-parser","summary":"Handle null as an empty string and preserve string trimming within src/parser.mjs only.","targets":["src/parser.mjs"],"title":"Null-safe parser","validation":["Run node scripts/verify.mjs unchanged to prove parse(